# DFlash Console — restart and UI refresh

When you finish a task that changed any of these, **automatically restart the Console server** before ending your turn:

- `api/**` or `core/**` (Python backend)
- `config.json`
- `requirements.txt`

## How to restart

From the repo root:

```powershell
.\scripts\restart-console-server.ps1
```

Use `.\run.ps1` only for a full cold start (first run, dependency install, or llama-server port cleanup).

## Static UI changes (no restart needed)

Changes under `static/**`, `static/css/**`, or `assets/**` do **not** require a server restart.

An open browser tab on `http://127.0.0.1:8900/` **auto-refreshes within ~2 seconds** when UI files change (`server-reload-watch.js` polls `/api/health` `ui_version`). Do **not** ask the user to hard-refresh manually after UI edits when the dev server is running.

After backend restart, the same watcher reloads on a new `boot_id`. No manual refresh needed in either case.

## After restart

Confirm the API is up (HTTP 200 from `http://127.0.0.1:8900/` or the configured `ui_port`). Do not ask the user to restart manually when you can run the script yourself.

When verifying UI work yourself, reload or open the Console in the browser rather than assuming the user already sees your changes.

## Browser verification (required after UI changes)

After **any** change under `static/**`, `static/css/**`, or `assets/**`:

1. Open `http://127.0.0.1:8900/` (Models tab → DFlash stacks when relevant).
2. Wait for auto-refresh (~2s) or navigate fresh.
3. **Take a browser screenshot** and confirm the change is visible (e.g. gold frame on ready-to-load stacks, deep green on selected rows).
4. Do **not** tell the user a UI fix is done until the screenshot shows it working.
